RESOURCE MANAGEMENT -- VILLAGE BUDGET ALLOCATION SUMMARY
Kazekage Office, treasury division, fiscal cycle

This summary records how the funding drawn from the Wind Daimyo and mission
commissions is allocated across the village's needs. Figures are apportioned by
share, not coin, in open record.

Allocation of record (by share):
- Water infrastructure and rationing (wells, cisterns, caravan escort of water):
  the largest single share, for water is the village's survival.
- Puppet Brigade and Workshop (components, poison stock, maintenance): a major
  share befitting the village's signature art.
- Wind-user and general shinobi provisioning (weapons, training, deployment).
- Academy and new-shinobi onboarding.
- Medical corps (heat-exposure care, field medicine).
- Reserve against sandstorm loss, caravan raids, and Daimyo funding shortfall --
  a lesson of the years when funding was cut.

The Kazekage Office reviews allocation each cycle. Prudence in scarcity is the
Sand's oldest discipline. Sealed to the treasury.
